{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Gold and silver and copper, etc.</b> All of them came as a freewill offering — each man whatever his heart volunteered — except for the silver, which came equally, a half-shekel for each person. And we do not find in all the work of the Mishkan that more silver was needed there, as it says, ״וְכֶסֶף פְּקוּדֵי הָעֵדָה וְגוֹ׳ בֶּקַע לַגֻּלְגֹּלֶת וְגוֹ׳״ (Exodus 38:25–26), and the rest of the silver that came there as a freewill offering they made into service vessels."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:21.779045861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}